    <statement><p>Compute the partial derivative:</p>
<p><m>f(x,y)=\sin\mathopen{}\left(x^{6}-3y\right)</m></p>
<p><m>f_{y}(0,\pi)=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>y</m>, using the Chain Rule. This gives:



<m>f_{y}(x,y)=\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^{6}-3y\right) \frac{\partial}{\partial{y}}\left(x^{6}-3y\right)=-3\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^{6}-3y\right)</m>



Evaluating at <m>(0,\pi)</m> we obtain



<m>f_{y}(0,\pi)=3</m>





</solution>
